<title>SOUTH AFRICA: King Food shares dip as talks called off.</title>
<headline>King Food shares dip as talks called off.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in King Food Holdings dipped to 160 cents from 170 on Friday after the firm said that negotiations first announced on April 16 had been called off.</p>
<p>&quot;The company issued a cautionary this morning, that's why they are down,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>However, by 1200 GMT the stock had recovered to 168 in trade of 30,000.</p>
</text>
